{"body":{"text":["The session built the engine's whole asking each store its whole question first, held to the seven conditions, with tests for divergence and for parts kept in another store, and a brief read with all its sections in one read, following only parts. Measured in the browser under like conditions, neither helped: the published site settled in 85 to 155 ms, the engine's change alone in 280 to 370, both together about 175, the richer read paying for the functions it applies. It reverted both, the tests passing. With the author's word, it found most passes are the engine learning its own vocabulary on every read, each function used, its type, its inputs and their types, and the kinds of value, about eight rounds before any work, and named a native vocabulary known once as the next session's ground. It kept the session and pushed."]},"id":"1M82SEZKRB9M000","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
